# Secrets — never commit
.env
*.key
*_token*

# Third-party screenplay text. The reconstruction pipeline reads a copyrighted
# screenplay to derive structure; it stores results BY REFERENCE (offsets and
# anchors) and never copies the prose. These files are the local working copies
# of that source text and must not leave this machine.
# Any run directory, not just reconstruct/. A new pipeline created
# distill/runs/ and the narrower pattern did not cover it, so a full screenplay
# was committed. Match by filename anywhere in the tree.
**/script.normalized.txt
**/script.raw.txt
**/runs/*/prose/
reconstruct/runs/*/script.normalized.txt
reconstruct/runs/*/prose/
**/matrix.txt
**/*_screenplay.txt
**/*.pdf
# Reference papers this project builds on are meant to ship. Explicit exception rather than
# a narrowed pattern: narrowing the screenplay rule is how a full script reached history once.
!reference/CogniTino-whitepaper.pdf

# Model weights and inference scratch
models/
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.bin

# Per-call logs: these carry full model responses and, for sighted calls, may
# quote source text. Structure is committed; raw call traffic is not.
**/logs/calls/
**/logs/*.json

# Intermediate repair snapshots — noise, and they can be large
**/artifacts/*.pre-repair*.json
**/quarantine/

# Generated viewers (rebuildable from artifacts with `narrativeforge site`)
runs/*/site
runs/api-grok/site/
webapp/*.html.bak

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

# Third-party books and source documents. The craft sheet in narrativeforge/craft.py
# is our own distillation of these; the sources themselves are not ours to publish.
How_to_Write_Damn_Good_Novel*.txt
frey*.pdf
frey*.txt
narrative-decomposition-whitepaper.pdf
plotemb.txt

# Rebuildable viewers and archives — large, and regenerable from artifacts
site/
archive/
*.tar.gz

# Derived corpora from the reconstruction runs. These carry no source prose — the KU and
# abstraction layers are gated on verbatim overlap — but the project's own copyright
# position is to ship the method and withhold the corpus, and these are the corpus. They
# were untracked rather than ignored, which meant one `git add -A` away from being
# committed. Structure travels in docs/; the run trees stay local.
runs/ku_*/
runs/cognitino_*/
runs/v4_enriched/
runs/v4_ornith*/
runs/v4_qwen_fresh/
.github/workflows/
